    summary:
      "T168 (MINORS-RESIST, 39/39, 2.3 s, the same 63-window union as T163–T167, recipe untouched, h = 96–1371; T167's scalar reproduced bit-compatibly before it is attacked (1 − r₁₂² = 1.28e-7–4.53e-4, h^−2.921 on frame A); κ = 0.038821 verified at every jump point up to n = 400000 — the ONE unconditional input) — contract LAGRANGE.MINORS: attack R1 through the Lagrange identity, the determinant as a sum of squares. (1) THE ANATOMY, ALL EXACT: Q = XᵀAX with X = [u, v] the two lowest parity modes in the A-metric (3.9e-15); the mode vectors are closed trigonometry, m-free, and EUCLIDEAN-ORTHOGONAL (the Euclidean r₁₂ is 0 to 6.2e-17, ‖u‖² = 1/μ₁ exactly) — the near-parallelism r₁₂² = 1 − O(h^−3) is created ENTIRELY by the arithmetic metric A and not at all by the vectors; the Wronskian telescopes exactly (W_r − W_{r−1} = (μ₁−μ₂)u_r v_r, 1.7e-13; the telescope closes at the window edge to 2.7e-18), so the near-diagonal minors are ONE closed one-parameter family — a Dirichlet partial sum; the minor sup is closed and m-free (~N/π², attained to 0.770); Cauchy–Binet is verified as algebra (1.1e-15 on random indefinite A) — the second compound of A is the exact kernel of the Lagrange form. (2) THE FINDING: on all 63 windows the h×h arithmetic kernel A is POSITIVE DEFINITE (λ_min = 5.0e-6–8.5e-4, 8–12 orders above the solver floor), so the second compound is PSD and det Q is a sum of squares with STRICTLY POSITIVE weights — ρ_LAG = S₊/det Q = 1.000 exactly, no sign cancellation anywhere. Hard fence, stated with the finding: this is a statement about one finite matrix per window, certified on THIS surface (h ≤ 1371); the Weil criterion is not tested, not assumed, not reverse-inferred. (3) THE KEY MEASUREMENT — IT SPLITS BY BASIS: in the closed basis the minors are MAXIMAL (½Σ M² = ‖u‖²‖v‖² − ⟨u,v⟩² = 1/(μ₁μ₂) EXACTLY (6.9e-16), ~ h⁴, 2.2e5–9.1e9 — the Wronskians carry ZERO arithmetic and the largest norm they could have: all smallness sits in the PSD kernel evaluated at one closed vector); in the eigenbasis the sum is THIN (90% of the weighted sum of squares from 4–101 pairs, ≤ 8e-4 of the h² eigen-pairs; the top pair is always (λ_min, λ_max) carrying 6.8–41.7% alone; and the pairs are RAW — κ_w = 0.30–0.94, a typical minor cancels only ~100:1): no internal cancellation, the thinness is the story. (4) THE EXPONENT LEDGER CLOSES, arithmetic-free: 1 − r₁₂² = ν₁ν₂/(â₁₁â₂₂) (1.0e-9, Poincaré separation) with ν₁ ~ h^+0.81, â₁₁ ~ h^+0.76, â₂₂ ~ h^+0.91, ν₂ ~ h^−1.38 — every factor but ONE at the right power. The best m-free-shaped bound B1 = λ₁λ₂/(â₁₁â₂₂) reads h^−0.548 on the union / h^−0.880 on frame A against the required h^−3 — short by h^2.45/h^2.04; the literal count-times-sup budget costs h^+2.049, twelve orders above target, closed so it is never tried again. The open factor is identified EXACTLY: ν₂, with minimiser t* = Q₁₂/Q₁₁ (factor 1.0000), needed to relative accuracy 6.05e-3 median / 2.82e-4 worst, sharpening h^−1.146 — T167 measured the SAME requirement from the other end (1.25e-5/3.19e-8 on r₁₂²): by T168-TH7 this factor IS the target rewritten — the Lagrange route does not lower the accuracy demand, it relocates it from a 2×2 determinant onto ONE RATIO, at the same price (which is why ONE-TERM-MISSING is deliberately NOT rendered: it would misread a reduction as progress on the inequality). No closed constant candidate works (1/√2 misses by up to 0.194 relative; t* drifts h^+0.076 over 0.570–0.790 — no h-independent constant can be the answer), no single-mode trial (the preregistered sine family overshoots λ_min by 285–1.5e6), the ground state is only 0.982-confined in the median (δ = 4.8e-4–0.41 does NOT decay, h^+0.059 — reported as a LIMIT, not support), and the Turán band is neither sign-definite nor telescoping. (5) CHAIN + STRESS: 1/g₂ = Q₁₁(1 − r₁₂²) verified to 1.2e-8 on 63/63, g₁₆ ≥ g₂ (Schur 1917) — the bounds transport with no extra step; certified end-to-end gain ≥ 1.00–2.13 (weak, valid, direction-verified). THE SCRAMBLE BREAKS HARDER THAN T167: 8/8 windows lose A ≻ 0 (n_neg up to 73) AND the 2×2 Gram property AND the Cholesky cascade — no window survives, and on those windows the Lagrange identity is no longer a sum of squares at all; the L_P control has Q₁₂ = 0 and 1 − r₁₂² = 1 exactly, the sum collapsing onto its diagonal pair — the arithmetic content is precisely what populates the off-diagonal minors; KMS/Dirichlet/correlation controls exact. THE CONCLUSION: the hardness is SELF-SIMILAR under exact reformulation — determinant → PSD compound at a closed vector → near-null Rayleigh value → one ratio of two closed lag sums, same accuracy price — and the seven no-gos say that no position-blind budget, no m-free trial vector, no h-independent constant and no count-times-sup budget can pay it. Balance: 8 THEOREM / 0 CERT-UNIF / 3 CERT-WINDOW / 11 MEASURED / 7 NO-GO. T169 (TSTAR.RATIO, tstar_ratio_probe.py, running) attacks the one factor as a preregistered candidate table. No promotion (candidates PENDING — bundling planned). Sandbox; not RH evidence.",
